<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="VARSPD2_AOI" Revision="2.2" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2007-09-14T17:41:17.040Z" CreatedBy="AOI Library" EditedDate="2026-10-29T20:57:04.002Z" EditedBy="AOI Library" SoftwareRevision="v38.01"
>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[3/10/21: Updated extended tag properties for AOIs local tags (lo, hi, and eng unit)

8/24/21: Add unlatch bits for scada manual start/stop and fail reset bits

10/29/26: Added START_scdi and STOP_scdi (latched start/stop status bits) with their latch logic; added SpeedRef_scai (speed reference from an external system, display only, no logic).

10/29/26: Parameters (inputs then outputs) and local tags sorted alphabetically; five local tags renamed with a leading underscore (_ENABLE_PB_scdo, _DISABLE_PB_scdo, _ENABLE_hwdo, _MonthRun_Hours_Reset_ONS, _Stuck_On_Alm_tmr); PLC - to - SCADA / SCADA - to - PLC added to descriptions of s-suffix parameters.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[AutoCall Interlock Inputs

INTRLK_scdi
Standard enable interlock.
1 = AutoCall enabled (RUN_hwdo, _ENABLE_hwdo)
0 = AutoCall disabled

AutoCall_INTRLK_scdi
Inverse enable interlock.
1 = AutoCall disabled
0 = AutoCall enabled

Notes
Both inputs control the same AutoCall functions.
They use opposite logic conventions (enable vs. disable true).
In most cases, use only one input and derive the other if needed.
Avoid conflicting states if both are used.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
